1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:04,470
Averaging means adding to a trade, to change your average price.

2
00:00:06,830 --> 00:00:11,810
You buy 1 lot of gold at $4,000. Every $1 move = $100.

3
00:00:12,360 --> 00:00:15,310
Gold drops $40, to $3,960. You're $4,000 down.

4
00:00:18,230 --> 00:00:20,880
You buy twice your position: 2 more lots at $3,960.

5
00:00:21,430 --> 00:00:25,440
With 3 lots, your average price is $3,973.33.

6
00:00:28,230 --> 00:00:32,940
To break even, gold now only needs +$13.33, not +$40.

7
00:00:33,490 --> 00:00:35,490
Each $1 is now worth $300.

8
00:00:38,270 --> 00:00:42,850
Move needed = loss ÷ (total lots × $100)

9
00:00:43,400 --> 00:00:47,610
2 lots: $20 · 3 lots: $13.33 · 4 lots: $10

10
00:00:50,670 --> 00:00:54,350
But if gold falls another $20, you're $10,000 down.

11
00:00:54,900 --> 00:00:57,920
Set a maximum size and a stop loss first.
